  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Cursed Spirit Manipulation — Innate Technique (11th level)</em></p><p>When you reach 11th level, as an action you can put any number of your cursed spirits in a spiral-like pattern(minimum 2), making them into a dark spiral that you can use in an attack. Every creature in a 30-foot cone must make a Dexterity saving throw, on a success they take half damage, on a failure they take 2d12 Necrotic damage.<br />\n For every cursed spirit above 2, the area of effect will be increased by 5 feet, and the damage will increase by 1d12.<br />\n All of the cursed spirits that were used in the Uzumaki are killed. However, you can obtain the actions(including legendary actions)they have at a cost which must be paid when extracting them via <em>Uzumaki</em>. You can extract multiple actions from different curses as part of the process, but you must pay the cost for each action.<br />\n The cost for the actions is listed below and once extracted, the action can be used only once:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Action Type</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Cursed Energy Cost</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus Action</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Action</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reactions</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Legendary Actions</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">10</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
   "chat": ""
  },
